Mr. Speaker, the From Surfaces to Services report came out in 2017. It said this province needed one coordinated approach to public transportation, and eight years on, nothing meaningful has been done with it. Nobody in this building owns the file. A minister who owned it would set the direction, sign the cheques, and answer to us here when the buses don't run. What we have instead is a handful of municipal transit systems, two ferry runs, school buses parked in a lot from nine until two, the vans the nursing homes send out, and a woman in my riding who drives her neighbour to dialysis twice a week because there is nothing else.

BE IT THEREFORE RESOLVED that the Legislative Assembly urge the Premier to give the Minister of Transportation and Infrastructure a mandate for public transportation;

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the Legislative Assembly urge the government to allocate the resources and the funding the New Brunswick Transportation Authority needs to write a public transportation strategy and then carry it out.

Madam Speaker, the motion reads as follows.

WHEREAS the 2017 From Surfaces to Services report identified the critical need for a comprehensive, coordinated approach to improving public transportation across the province, yet no meaningful action has been taken;

I repeat: no meaningful action has been taken. Eight years.

WHEREAS appointing a Minister responsible for public transportation would provide the leadership, the coordination and the accountability needed to develop, fund and integrate public transportation services throughout New Brunswick;

BE IT THEREFORE RESOLVED that the Legislative Assembly urge the Premier to give the Minister of Transportation and Infrastructure a mandate for public transportation;

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the Legislative Assembly urge the government to allocate the necessary resources and funding to support the New Brunswick Transportation Authority to create and implement a public transportation strategy.

A mandate. That is the word in the motion, and I will say it again -- a mandate. Not a study. The report is written. It has been written since 2017.
